    course_description = '<h4>Overview</h4><p>Our General English courses are designed for international students and other temporary visa holders looking to improve their English for personal or professional development. You can study this course by itself (stand-alone) or as part of a package with another ELICOS or TAFE SA course. The course will be tailored to your individual needs, depending on your level of English, goals and study pathway, and will focus on: - Developing listening, speaking, reading and writing skills - Improving vocabulary and grammar - Developing communication skills - Introduction to Australian culture and accent You can start your study weekly, with a short pre-course assessment and interview to ensure you are enrolled at a level that suits you.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 40,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 16080,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>Satisfactory completion of <a href="https://www.tafesa.edu.au/international/entry-requirements">Year 10 or overseas equivalent</a> .</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Academic <a href="https://www.tafesa.edu.au/international/entry-requirements">IELTS score</a> of 6.0 Overall with minimum of 5.0 in all bands or equivalent.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
